# Agent orchestration — lean path (default)

Full guide: `prompts/guides/agent_orchestration_minimal_harness_v1.md`.

## Default (almost all work)

```text
Auto / @coder | @designer | @planner → edit → validate-report on build/test
```

- Prefer **one owner**, flat modules, direct exec. No speculative wrappers or multi-agent scaffolding.
- Do **not** spawn Task trees, `@orchestrator`, `@flow-controller`, or ops scans unless a trigger below matches.
- Skill parity: sync/read `agent-lang` only if empty/stale — not a full BLANG boot for every typo.

## Opt-in triggers (then use the full tools)

| Trigger | Then |
|:---|:---|
| Spawning Task/subagents or multi-step multi-owner work | `agent_flow_route` → follow phases |
| HANDOFF lease / program slice / multi-domain | `driver.mjs boot <agent>` |
| Product queue row close (`exit_predicate`) | **WIT-HON → WIT → Q✓** (mandatory) |
| MCP art program | `@orchestrator-mcp` lane (not engine `@orchestrator`) |
| Task quota fail-cycle | `@main-thread-orchestrator` / foreground `@coder` |
| Lane close / pre-architecture / supervisor review | `@operations-intelligence` |
| Explicit parallel secondary vs P1 | `@coparent-orchestrator` |

## Never thin away

validation-first · witness spine · WIT-HON before product Q✓ · consumer vs `*-mcp` · bevy-simulation-grade authority
